  "divergences": [
    "src/alienclaw_ga/evolution/types.py: the TYPE_CHECKING import of alienclaw.brains.types.BrainSpec (DROP) is replaced by alienclaw_ga.genome.schema.DirectedMutationSpec (a Protocol); EvolutionConfig.brain keeps its name, default None and runtime behavior, only its annotation changed.",
    "src/alienclaw_ga/genome/schema.py (new, extracted): ParameterSchemaField copied field-for-field from alienclaw.brains.types; BrainSpec replaced by the DirectedMutationSpec/ParameterFieldLike Protocols plus a minimal MutationSchema dataclass. mutate_directed only reads .parameter_schema, so in-tree BrainSpec objects still work.",
    "src/alienclaw_ga/numeric.py (new, extracted): clamp01 copied verbatim from alienclaw.fitness.function; the retired composition scorer evaluate() and alienclaw.fitness.types are not staged. evolution.generation, diagnostics.fixation_theory and diagnostics.per_genome_capture import clamp01 from alienclaw_ga.numeric.",
    "Every alienclaw.X reference (imports, mock.patch target strings, docstring module names) is rewritten to alienclaw_ga.X; ruff re-sorted the import block of evolution/generation.py where the rewrite changed the isort order.",
    "Ported diagnostics tests: ruff --fix removed unused imports (math, numpy, os, CaptureTrace, is_enabled) and re-sorted import blocks; one over-long line in test_dynamics_summary.py was wrapped. In-tree test/diagnostics is outside the CI ruff scope, the staged copy is linted.",
    "tests/genome/test_step_mutation.py and tests/evolution/test_generation.py build MutationSchema instead of BrainSpec/GenomeSectionDocs; the parameter_schema contents are unchanged.",
    "tests/genome/test_genome_vectors.py resolves the fixture from tests/fixtures/ instead of <repo>/test/fixtures/.",
    "tests/diagnostics/test_dynamics_summary.py reproduces option_b and option_current locally because diagnostics.fitness_formula_candidates is excluded; finite-input math is identical.",
    "tests/diagnostics/test_instrumentation.py drives the record_* producers directly instead of through alienclaw.bridge.server.handle; test_production_response_identical_when_off and test_decoded_params_reach_runner (bridge behavior) are dropped and test_capture_deactivated_after_block is added.",
    "Lint config: diagnostics sources keep their math-style names (N, H_x, X_obs) and the public CaptureHook() name via per-file N802/N803/N806 ignores (plus E501 for genome_information.py), so those copies stay verbatim apart from import rewrites.",
    "Unchanged on purpose for tuner compatibility: ALIENCLAW_POPULATIONS_ROOT and the ~/.alienclaw/populations default in evolution/storage.py, the ALIENCLAW_DIAGNOSTICS flag, the 'martian_type' naming throughout, and the RunMartianCallback alias.",
    "Comments and docstrings that point at in-tree files are left as-is, e.g. the src/alienclaw/registry/genome-codec.ts TS mirror in genome/*, bridge/server.py as the instrumentation producer, and '# list[Optional[BrainSpec]]' in operators.mutate_directed.",
    "New, not derived from a source: src/alienclaw_ga/__init__.py, tests/__init__.py, tests/conftest.py (pins HOME and ALIENCLAW_POPULATIONS_ROOT to tmp_path, disables the Hypothesis example database), tests/test_tuner_contract.py, tests/test_no_drop_imports.py, pyproject.toml, README.md.",
    "2026-11-26 (review follow-up): mutual_information's bias term is now Miller-Madow, MI_plugin - (m_joint - m_x - m_y + 1) / (2N), floored at 0; the old term (m_x * m_y - m_joint - 1) / (2N) and PKT-1477's min(raw_mi, corrected) clamp are gone, and the local names H_x/H_y/H_joint became h_x/h_y/h_joint (ruff-clean in-tree). Applied to both sides: genome_information.py is still verbatim, tests/diagnostics/test_mi_bias_correction.py still differs only by the import rewrite."
  ]
}
